% (also the name of a fabric), "parka" (with the overcoats in the European
% notes; no US text found), "twinset" (two garments), "earmuffs" and
% "wristband" (no kind of the rules), plastic headbands and hair clips
% (heading 9615 in US rulings, 3926 in the European notes).
"car coat" is a word for the kind carcoat,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "Men's or boys' overcoats, car coats, capes, cloaks, anoraks (including ski jackets), windcheaters, wind-jackets and similar articles".
"car coats" is a word for the kind carcoat,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "Men's or boys' overcoats, car coats, capes, cloaks, anoraks (including ski jackets), windcheaters, wind-jackets and similar articles".
"windcheater" is a word for the kind windbreaker,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "Men's or boys' overcoats, car coats, capes, cloaks, anoraks (including ski jackets), windcheaters, wind-jackets and similar articles".
"windcheaters" is a word for the kind windbreaker,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "Men's or boys' overcoats, car coats, capes, cloaks, anoraks (including ski jackets), windcheaters, wind-jackets and similar articles".
"wind-jacket" is a word for the kind windbreaker,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "Men's or boys' overcoats, car coats, capes, cloaks, anoraks (including ski jackets), windcheaters, wind-jackets and similar articles".
"wind-jackets" is a word for the kind windbreaker,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "Men's or boys' overcoats, car coats, capes, cloaks, anoraks (including ski jackets), windcheaters, wind-jackets and similar articles".
"blouson" is a word for the kind windbreaker,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 62, confer "Wind-jackets (commonly referred to as ‘blousons’) are outer garments covering the upper part of the body.".
"blousons" is a word for the kind windbreaker,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 62, confer "Wind-jackets (commonly referred to as ‘blousons’) are outer garments covering the upper part of the body.".
"pyjamas" is a word for the kind pajamas,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "Men's or boys' underpants, briefs, nightshirts, pyjamas, bathrobes, dressing gowns and similar articles, knitted or crocheted".
"pyjama" is a word for the kind pajamas,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "Men's or boys' underpants, briefs, nightshirts, pyjamas, bathrobes, dressing gowns and similar articles, knitted or crocheted".
"babydoll" is a word for the kind pajamas,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "which consist of a very short nightdress and matching briefs, are also considered to be pyjamas".
"babydolls" is a word for the kind pajamas,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "which consist of a very short nightdress and matching briefs, are also considered to be pyjamas".
"turtleneck" is a word for the kind pullover,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "Lightweight fine knit roll, polo or turtleneck jumpers and pullovers".
"turtlenecks" is a word for the kind pullover,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "Lightweight fine knit roll, polo or turtleneck jumpers and pullovers".
"hairband" is a word for the kind headband,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 96, confer "are classified as clothing accessories under heading 6117 or 6217".
"hairbands" is a word for the kind headband,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 96, confer "are classified as clothing accessories under heading 6117 or 6217".
% Babies' garments by their name (heading 6111 of the European notes)
"christening robe" is a word for a garment for babies,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "1. christening robes and gowns;".
"christening robes" is a word for a garment for babies,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "1. christening robes and gowns;".
"christening gown" is a word for a garment for babies,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "1. christening robes and gowns;".
"christening gowns" is a word for a garment for babies,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "1. christening robes and gowns;".
"pixie suit" is a word for a garment for babies,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "pixie suits: garments with hoods and sleeves, forming both a coat and a bag".
"pixie suits" is a word for a garment for babies,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "pixie suits: garments with hoods and sleeves, forming both a coat and a bag".
"romper bag" is a word for a garment for babies,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "romper bags for babies, which may also be padded".
"romper bags" is a word for a garment for babies,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "romper bags for babies, which may also be padded".
"quilted wrap" is a word for a garment for babies,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "They include: coats, cloaks, quilted wraps, pixie suits, dressing gowns".
"quilted wraps" is a word for a garment for babies,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "They include: coats, cloaks, quilted wraps, pixie suits, dressing gowns".
% Knitted fabrics
"single jersey" is a fabric of construction knitted,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "Single jersey (plain knit) is the simplest form of weft knit".
"plain knit" is a fabric of construction knitted,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "Single jersey (plain knit) is the simplest form of weft knit".
"weft knit" is a fabric of construction knitted,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "Single jersey (plain knit) is the simplest form of weft knit".
"ribbed knit" is a fabric of construction knitted,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "Lightweight roll, polo or turtleneck jumpers and pullovers are usually knitted in single jersey (plain knit), ribbed knit (1 × 1) or interlock.".
"fine knit" is a fabric of construction knitted,
    as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61, confer "Lightweight roll, polo or turtleneck jumpers and pullovers are usually knitted in single jersey (plain knit), ribbed knit (1 × 1) or interlock.".
"tricot" is a fabric of construction knitted,
    as stated in the coated apparel publication, confer "an open construction such as a tricot knit or mesh".
"tricot knit" is a fabric of construction knitted,
    as stated in the coated apparel publication, confer "an open construction such as a tricot knit or mesh".
"knit to shape" is a fabric of construction knitted,
    as stated in the knit to shape publication, confer "the term “knit to shape” means garments knit to shape on flat-knitting machines".
% Coated fabrics of Chapter 59
"leathercloth" is a fabric of heading 5903,
    as stated in ruling HQ H310888, confer "be embossed to simulate, e.g., the grain of leather (“leathercloth”)".
"flocked fabric" is a fabric of heading 5907,
    as stated in the coated apparel publication, confer "flocking will because flocked fabric is provided for in heading 5907".
"flocked fabrics" is a fabric of heading 5907,
    as stated in the coated apparel publication, confer "flocking will because flocked fabric is provided for in heading 5907".

rule kind_by_name with provenance the apparel terminology publication,
        confer "Apparel Terminology under the HTSUS":
the kind of a good is a kind
    if the good is called a name
    and the name is a word for the kind the kind.

rule kind_by_field with provenance the listing format,
        confer "Item Type (64 listings): the kind of product in the seller's words":
the kind of a good is a kind
    if the field a field of the good reads a value
    and the field is a field that names the kind
    and the value is a word for the kind the kind.

rule specific_kind_by_name with provenance the apparel terminology publication,
        confer "Tops (6114) - are upper body garments that are not included more specifically in headings 6101-6113":
a good is named by a specific kind
    if the good is called a name
    and the name is a word for the kind a kind.

rule specific_kind_by_field with provenance the apparel terminology publication,
        confer "Tops (6114) - are upper body garments that are not included more specifically in headings 6101-6113":
a good is named by a specific kind
    if the field a field of the good reads a name
    and the field is a field that names the kind
    and the name is a word for the kind a kind.

rule residual_kind_by_name with provenance the apparel terminology publication,
        confer "Tops (6114) - are upper body garments that are not included more specifically in headings 6101-6113":
the kind of a good is a kind
    if the good is called a name
    and the name is a word for the residual kind the kind
    and it is not the case that
        the good is named by a specific kind.

rule residual_kind_by_field with provenance the apparel terminology publication,
        confer "Tops (6114) - are upper body garments that are not included more specifically in headings 6101-6113":
the kind of a good is a kind
    if the field a field of the good reads a name
    and the field is a field that names the kind
    and the name is a word for the residual kind the kind
    and it is not the case that
        the good is named by a specific kind.

rule construction_by_fabric with provenance the apparel terminology publication,
        confer "constructed from lightweight, plain jersey or interlock knit fabric":
the fabric construction of a garment is a construction
    if the garment is made of the fabric a name
    and the name is a fabric of construction the construction.

rule construction_by_fabric_field with provenance the listing format,
        confer "Fabric Type (38 listings): the name of the fabric":
the fabric construction of a garment is a construction
    if the field a field of the garment reads a name
    and the field is a field that names the fabric
    and the name is a fabric of construction the construction.

rule fabric_heading_by_fabric with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Garments, made up of fabrics of heading 5602, 5603, 5903, 5906 or 5907":
a garment is made up of fabric of heading a heading
    if the garment is made of the fabric a name
    and the name is a fabric of heading the heading.

rule fabric_heading_by_field with provenance the listing format,
        confer "Fabric Type (38 listings): the name of the fabric":
a garment is made up of fabric of heading a heading
    if the field a field of the garment reads a name
    and the field is a field that names the fabric
    and the name is a fabric of heading the heading.

% Not a rule: "Craft of Weaving: Non-Woven" is not read as the fabric of
% heading 5603. Shops write it on woven garments, and the fabric heading
% sends a garment to heading 6210 (RatioTariff §3.15). A fabric named
% nonwoven still gives the heading (fabric_heading_by_name).

rule compression_by_name with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Graduated compression hosiery (for example, stockings for varicose veins)":
a good is graduated compression hosiery
    if the good is called a name
    and the name is a word for graduated compression hosiery.

rule compression_by_field with provenance the listing format,
        confer "Item Type (64 listings): the kind of product in the seller's words":
a good is graduated compression hosiery
    if the field a field of the good reads a name
    and the field is a field that names the kind
    and the name is a word for graduated compression hosiery.

rule terry_by_fabric with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Terry cloth type, looped pile fabric":
the fabric of a garment is terry
    if the garment is made of the fabric a name
    and the name is a terry fabric.

rule terry_by_field with provenance the listing format,
        confer "Fabric Type (38 listings): the name of the fabric":
the fabric of a garment is terry
    if the field a field of the garment reads a name
    and the field is a field that names the fabric
    and the name is a terry fabric.

rule napped_by_fabric with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Jersey type, brushed or napped fabric":
a garment is napped
    if the garment is made of the fabric a name
    and the name is a napped fabric.

rule napped_by_field with provenance the listing format,
        confer "Fabric Type (38 listings): the name of the fabric":
a garment is napped
    if the field a field of the garment reads a name
    and the field is a field that names the fabric
    and the name is a napped fabric.

% note 6(a) of Chapter 61 (and note 5(a) of Chapter 62): babies' garments are
% for a body height of 86 centimetres or less
rule babies_by_height with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "The expression \"babies' garments and clothing accessories\" means articles for young children of a body height not exceeding 86 centimeters":
a garment is sized for babies
    if the garment is made for a body height of a number centimetres
    and the number =< 86.

rule babies_by_name with provenance the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 61,
        confer "if they are clearly identifiable as garments meant for babies":
a garment is sized for babies
    if the garment is called a name
    and the name is a word for a garment for babies.

rule babies_by_field with provenance the listing format,
        confer "Item Type (64 listings): the kind of product in the seller's words":
a garment is sized for babies
    if the field a field of the garment reads a name
    and the field is a field that names the kind
    and the name is a word for a garment for babies.

scenario european_notes is:
    coat one is called "car coats".
    the field "item type" of jacket one reads "blouson".
    nightwear is called "pyjamas".
    gown one is called "christening gown".
    the field "item type" of bag one reads "romper bag".
    top one is made of the fabric "single jersey".
    jacket two is made of the fabric "leathercloth".
    european_kinds expects answers ["the kind of coat one is carcoat", "the kind of jacket one is windbreaker", "the kind of nightwear is pajamas"].
    european_babies expects answers ["gown one is sized for babies", "bag one is sized for babies"].
    european_constructions expects answers ["the fabric construction of top one is knitted"].
    european_headings expects answers ["jacket two is made up of fabric of heading 5903"].

query european_kinds is:
    the kind of which good is which kind.

query european_babies is:
    which garment is sized for babies.

query european_constructions is:
    the fabric construction of which garment is which construction.

query european_headings is:
    which garment is made up of fabric of heading which heading.

scenario tee is:
    tee is called "t-shirt".
    tee is made of the fabric "jersey".
    hood is called "hoodie".
    the field "fabric type" of blouse reads "broadcloth".
    the field "item type" of skirt one reads "tops".
    the field "tops type" of tee reads "tops".
    kinds expects answers ["the kind of tee is T-shirt", "the kind of hood is pullover", "the kind of skirt one is top"].
    constructions expects answers ["the fabric construction of tee is knitted", "the fabric construction of blouse is woven"].

scenario outerwear is:
    shell is called "windbreaker".
    the field "item type" of wrap reads "shawls".
    shell is made of the fabric "nonwoven".
    outerwear expects answers ["the kind of shell is windbreaker", "the kind of wrap is shawl"].
    constructions expects answers ["the fabric construction of shell is nonwoven"].

scenario tariff_words is:
    sleeper is called "blanket sleepers".
    hose one is called "surgical stockings".
    the field "item type" of vest one reads "waistcoat".
    suit one is called "jogging suit".
    cape one is made of the fabric "felt".
    the field "craft of weaving" of gown reads "non-woven".
    towel tee is made of the fabric "terry cloth".
    the field "fabric type" of fleece reads "brushed".
    romper one is made for a body height of 80 centimetres.
    child is made for a body height of 110 centimetres.
    tariff_kinds expects answers ["the kind of sleeper is pajamas", "the kind of hose one is stockings", "the kind of vest one is vest", "the kind of suit one is track suit"].
    fabric_headings expects answers ["cape one is made up of fabric of heading 5602"].
    compression expects answers ["hose one is graduated compression hosiery"].
    terry expects answers ["the fabric of towel tee is terry"].
    napped expects answers ["fleece is napped"].
    babies expects answers ["romper one is sized for babies"].

query tariff_kinds is:
    the kind of which good is which kind.

query fabric_headings is:
    which garment is made up of fabric of heading which heading.

query compression is:
    which good is graduated compression hosiery.

query terry is:
    the fabric of which garment is terry.

query napped is:
    which garment is napped.

query babies is:
    which garment is sized for babies.

query outerwear is:
    the kind of which good is which kind.

query kinds is:
    the kind of which good is which kind.

query constructions is:
    the fabric construction of which garment is which construction.
